# claude-config repo — conservative-by-default
#
# Everything is ignored, then we re-add ONLY the files that are safe to
# version (settings + custom scripts). Transcripts, sessions, history,
# policy-limits, auth caches, paste-cache, telemetry, downloads, and
# backups all stay out — they may contain conversation content, file
# contents from your edits, rate-limit state, and other sensitive data.

# Default: ignore everything in this dir.
/*

# Allowlist: explicit re-includes go below.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/settings.json
!/statusline.sh

# If you start versioning custom agents/commands/hooks, uncomment:
# !/agents/
# !/commands/
# !/hooks/

# --- skills -------------------------------------------------------------
# Conservative: re-include the skills dir itself, re-ignore its contents,
# then allowlist individual skills. Marketplace/plugin skills stay out.
!/skills/
/skills/*
!/skills/swarm-loop/
!/skills/build-docs/

# ...but never bytecode or tool caches from inside a versioned skill.
/skills/swarm-loop/**/__pycache__/
/skills/swarm-loop/**/*.py[co]
/skills/swarm-loop/**/.pytest_cache/

# To version another skill, add:  !/skills/<name>/
